  "assessment": "Reconciled twelve direct interests, seven stable directions, thirty-one curricular topics, six illustrations and eleven individual outcomes. Eleven generator rows belong to the closest broad psychology/cognitive core. Clinical/developmental owns three, social/organisational three, methods one and clinical neuropsychology one. Every generator is accounted for; additional methods and neuropsychology priorities remain evidenced but unattempted after three. No residual omnibus cluster or inherited split-target evidence is used.",
  "sourceSupport": {
    "19928–19946": "The programme and its introductory course corroborate broad psychology, behaviour, cognition, development, mental health, social/work behaviour, research and individual differences. The dated seven study paths corroborate every stable direction. Dutch-only Clinical Neuropsychology remains legitimate for this bilingual target.",
    "19947–19977": "The inspected common courses, four Brain/Cognition courses and named methods/thesis entries corroborate cognitive/neuropsychology, development, social/work psychology, interviewing, psychometrics, experimental design, data science, writing, ethics and conceptual foundations. These topics support the concepts without generating extra alternatives. Clinical/developmental and organisational/social specialisation descriptions substantiate the related emphases.",
    "19978–19983": "Cognitive-load, social-pressure, mental-health, workplace-research, behavioural-data and childhood-memory questions remain examples and search-only terms, not additional compulsory courses or independent programme generators.",
    "19984–19994": "Postgraduate, research and employment outcomes remain conditional or individual search-only terms. The comparison grants no research-master admission, doctoral placement, clinical registration, psychological assessment entitlement or professional employment guarantee."
  },
